--- exp_memory_question.py ---
saved results/memory-question/run-2026-11-17T05-55-35.json
P_need=1: all 28 arm/read-budget combinations live to the horizon, so the medium gives no policy an advantage and the memory question is empty. P_need=2: the staying arm dies at step 24 while every arm that keeps moving lives 20000, so the question the medium does ask is 'move at all', not 'remember where'. The decisive number is that the oracle - which knows the globally richest cell at every step - lives exactly as long as the random walk (20000 against 20000 at read_budget=3, and the same at 0, 1 and 2), so perfect information about the field is worth zero over wandering. Memory cannot be worth more than information, so in this medium it is worth nothing. NOT APPLICABLE to 'does the medium pose a memory question': it does not, because on a uniform ring with income equal to upkeep any movement suffices and the richest cell is always adjacent. The partial-observability question only appears when the field is not uniform - which this grid does not contain.
