  M=2.0 r=0.825 income=0.6 m=0.5: S=1.6500 >= income (above)

floor(income/m) — целочисленный закон, но float-floor даёт 5 для
  0.6/0.1, а прогон даёт 6: шестой едок забирает оставшиеся 0.1.

  OK   fires     the sequential population saturates at the capacity the arithmetic predicted: on the 14 rungs above it, it holds exactly that capacity and does not grow with n. The reference is `reference_k_seq`, written separately from `k_sequential`. All three injected defects are caught: an arm that tracks n, a capacity off by one cell-load in either direction, and a capacity that ignores the field size. This shows the arm saturates where predicted; it does not prove the prediction, which `silent` checks against the same rows
  OK   silent    30/30 rungs match their own formula exactly (seq: min(n, cells*k_seq) with k_seq = floor(S/t) + [rem >= m]; prop: n if income/k >= m else 0), and the ladder goes above both thresholds (14 rungs above the sequential capacity, 16 above the proportional one), so neither control is silent by having nothing to see
  OK   specific  the protocols are limited by different things: sequential leaves 14 rungs with a partially-fed population (the field caps it), proportional leaves 0 -- it splits evenly, so it dies all at once (the organism caps it); the injected gradual death of the proportional arm is caught

