  the two protocols are limited by different quantities: sequential by the cell's supply, cells*(floor(M*r/income) + [remainder >= maintenance]); proportional by the organism's demand, cells*floor(income/maintenance). The proportional protocol holds more organisms because it rations each one down to maintenance. The saturation control is checked against a reference that does not use k_seq, and it rejects k_seq off by one in either direction

